  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Calculate ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+4\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x.$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-\\,$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+4\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+4(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
